# CLAUDE.md - template for a MATLAB/Simulink project

<!--
HOW TO USE THIS FILE
====================
Copy to your project root as CLAUDE.md, then replace every <angle-bracket> placeholder.
Delete sections that don't apply. Keep it under ~200 lines - it is loaded into every
session, and a long file dilutes the parts that matter.

THE PRINCIPLE: CLAUDE.md is not documentation. It is the set of things that are true
about this project and expensive to rediscover. Anything the agent can learn by reading
the code does NOT belong here. Anything that cost someone an afternoon does.

WHERE THIS FILE LIVES: if CLAUDE.md is gitignored, NOTHING in it reaches a colleague's
clone. Anything a human collaborator must know belongs in a TRACKED file as well.
-->

## What this is

<One paragraph: what the project is, who the client/stakeholder is, what the deliverable is.>

There is no build or test command - the code runs inside MATLAB/Simulink. The regression suite is
`<run_all_verify.m>`.

**What is deliberately NOT here:** <e.g. client correspondence and meeting material live in
OneDrive at ...>

## Read this first

**<PROJECT_INDEX.md>** - annotated file tree plus a "where to look, by question" table. Consult it
**before** searching or globbing; it will usually point straight at the right file.

<!-- An index like this is worth writing once. It converts a five-tool-call search into one read. -->

## Code map

<!-- Simulink projects have a discoverability problem: the behaviour is in .slx files the
     agent cannot read as text. This table is the fix. -->

| Layer | Path |
|---|---|
| Top-level model | `<TopModel>.slx` <if you keep variant models, name them and say what differs> |
| Subsystem libraries | `<models/*.slx>` |
| Algorithm bodies | `<functions/algorithms/*.m>` ← **the real logic lives here** |
| <Domain> primitives | `<functions/area/*.m>` |
| Pre-sim configuration | `<functions/preSim/*.m>` |
| Post-sim diagnostics | `<functions/postSim/*.m>` |

The `.slx` files are binary - **do not attempt to read or edit them as text.** To change behaviour,
edit the corresponding `.m` file, which is what the Simulink MATLAB Function blocks call.

<!-- Then any project-wide convention that is invisible from the code but assumed everywhere:
     an index or enum ordering, a units convention, a naming scheme, a sign convention.
     One line each. These are cheap to state and expensive for an agent to infer wrongly. -->

<e.g. "Index convention throughout: 1 = <first>, 2 = <second>, 3 = <third>.">
<e.g. "All timestamps are microseconds since power-on, uint64.">
<e.g. "Angles are radians internally; degrees only at the display boundary.">

## Which skills can actually run here

<!-- THE MOST IMPORTANT SECTION. The toolkit installs regardless of what you license.
     Without this table the agent attempts things it cannot do, and the failure surfaces
     three steps later as something confusing. Refresh it with detect_matlab_toolboxes. -->

Verified <date>. Installed and licensed: **<MATLAB, Simulink, ...>** - nothing else.

| Skill | Status | Blocker |
|---|---|---|
| `building-simulink-models`, `simulating-simulink-models`, the profiler/debugger skills, `managing-simulink-projects` | Usable | - |
| `specifying-mbd-algorithms`, `specifying-plant-models`, `filing-bug-reports` | Usable | Templates only, no toolbox needed |
| `generate-requirement-drafts` | Degraded | No Requirements Toolbox → use its **YAML fallback**, not `.slreqx` |
| `testing-simulink-models` | Degraded | No Simulink Test → no `sltest.TestCase`; use plain `sim` + `assert` |
| `checking-model-compliance`, `author-modeladvisor-checks` | **Blocked** | No Simulink Check → no Model Advisor |
| `building-architecture-models` | **Blocked** | No System Composer |
| Most MATLAB-catalog skills (RF, radar, wireless, robotics, image processing, …) | **Blocked** | Those toolboxes are not installed |

**When a skill is blocked, say so and stop - do not fake Model Advisor output or invent compliance
results.** `detect_matlab_toolboxes` settles any doubt in one call.

